---
description: Module Structure Guidelines
globs: "**/*.module.ts"
alwaysApply: true
---
- Organize module files in a consistent structure:
  ```
  src/
  └── entity/
      {{#if isGraphQL}}├── inputs/
      │   └── entity-*.input.ts
      └── objects/
      │   └── entity.object.ts{{/if}}
      {{#if isRest}}├── dto/
      │   └── entity-*.dto.ts{{/if}}
      ├── errors/
      │   ├── entity.errors.ts
      │   └── entity-*.error.ts
      ├── entity.module.ts
      {{#if isGraphQL}}├── entity.resolver.ts{{/if}}
      {{#if isRest}}├── entity.controller.ts{{/if}}
      ├── entity.service.ts
      {{#if isMongoose}}├── entity.repository.ts
      └── entity.schema.ts{{/if}}
      {{#if isPrisma}}└── (no repository/schema - using Prisma){{/if}}
  ```
- Each module must be self-contained with its own module definition, {{#if isGraphQL}}resolver{{/if}}{{#if isRest}}controller{{/if}}, service{{#if isMongoose}}, repository, and schema{{/if}} files
- Follow proper dependency injection: {{#if isGraphQL}}Resolvers{{/if}}{{#if isRest}}Controllers{{/if}} -> Services{{#if isMongoose}} -> Repositories -> Models{{/if}}{{#if isPrisma}} -> PrismaService{{/if}}
@module-template.ts
